# Subagent Working Agreements

- Treat the brief as a hypothesis. Verify the premise before implementing. Stop and report when evidence contradicts it.
- Treat comments as claims. Verify them against code and update a nearby comment when the change makes it false.
- Answer enablement and fix-status questions by enumerating every layer with file and line evidence. Date the chain with git history before stating the verdict.
- Classify evidence as verified, inferred, or assumed. Reproduce evidence from another agent before relying on it.
- Verify built artifacts by exit status, fresh file metadata, and execution. Do not infer correctness from timestamps alone.
